# Copy to .env and fill in real values (never commit real secrets).
DATABASE_URL="file:./dev.db"

# --- CI / E2E (no real secrets) -------------------------------------------
# GitHub Actions CI (see .github/workflows/ci.yml) sets ONLY a placeholder
# `DATABASE_URL="file:./ci.db"` — never real secrets. This is sufficient
# because:
#   - `prisma generate`, `next build` and `npm run dev` all work without
#     Supabase/Sentry/OpenAI envs (the app degrades gracefully: console error
#     reporter, signed-out profile fallback).
#   - The Playwright E2E suite (tests/*.spec.ts, run via `npm run test:e2e`)
#     covers UI flows only — localization, onboarding quiz, theme, keyboard,
#     ARIA, offline shell. None of them require auth or a real database.
#
# Flows that DO need real credentials are intentionally NOT part of CI E2E:
#   - POST /api/generate-program (AI program generation) requires a real
#     Supabase project (NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL + NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY)
#     for auth and an OpenAI API key (OPENAI_API_KEY, consumed by
#     @ai-sdk/openai). The GitHub Actions repository secret with this exact
#     name is injected into build/E2E jobs, but AI calls remain outside the
#     current UI-only E2E suite. Exercise AI generation locally / in staging.
#   - Sentry DSNs enable real error reporting; without them a console
#     reporter is used (src/lib/errorTracking.ts).
#
# If a future E2E test starts exercising auth or the DB, it must be gated on
# explicit env flags (e.g. `E2E_REQUIRES_AUTH=1`) and skipped transparently
# when unset — never silently hidden behind a mocked failure.

# --- PWA / TWA (required for Android release) ------------------------------
# Canonical production origin (HTTPS). Used for OG/social absolute URLs
# (generateMetadata metadataBase) and as the `host` origin of the Android
# Trusted Web Activity. Must match the deployed domain that serves
# /.well-known/assetlinks.json. See RELEASING.md.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://your-production-domain.example

# --- Monitoring (optional) -------------------------------------------------
# Error tracking: set a Sentry DSN to enable real error reporting. Requires
# the Sentry SDK to be installed (`npm i @sentry/nextjs`) — see
# src/lib/errorTracking.ts. Without a DSN the app uses a console reporter.
#
# Client-side (browser) errors:
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN=https://<key>@o<org>.ingest.sentry.io/<project>
# Server-side (Node) errors:
# SENTRY_DSN=https://<key>@o<org>.ingest.sentry.io/<project>

# --- AI rate limiting (shared storage) ------------------------------------
# Rate limiting for POST /api/generate-program (IP / user / daily windows +
# per-user concurrency) goes through a swappable store
# (src/lib/ai/rateLimitStore.ts). Choose the backend explicitly:
#
#   RATE_LIMIT_STORE=memory  (DEFAULT) — process-local fallback. Zero config,
#     no secrets, but NOT shared across instances and reset on restart. Fine
#     for local development.
#
#   RATE_LIMIT_STORE=redis  — shared, multi-instance-safe backend backed by an
#     Upstash REST-compatible Redis API (atomic INCR+EXPIRE windows and
#     SET NX PX concurrency locks). Requires BOTH REDIS_REST_URL and
#     REDIS_REST_TOKEN below. Never commit a real token — keep placeholders in
#     this file and inject the real values via the deployment environment.
#
# RATE_LIMIT_STORE=memory
# REDIS_REST_URL=https://your-project.upstash.io
# REDIS_REST_TOKEN=placeholder-token-do-not-commit
